;===========================================================
; 01d_params_lab.fis
;
; LABORATORY VALIDATION parameter set - own test programme.
;
; SEPARATE from 01_parameters.fis (Gai & Sanchez verification)
; and 01c_params_kennedy.fis (Kennedy 2023 external
; validation). Neither of those is modified. Never call more
; than ONE of the three parameter files in the same FLAC
; session - the second would silently overwrite the first.
;
; VARIABLE NAMING - IMPORTANT
; The names below are the ones 02_m_eicp.fis actually reads.
; They are not free to rename. Requested labels that differ:
;   $kappa_p  requested as $kappa_p   (same)
;   $m_cs     requested as $M_cs
;   $ds_p     requested as $Ds_p
;   $ini_e    requested as $ini_e
; FISH is case-insensitive so $M_cs and $Ds_p would in fact
; resolve, but the canonical spellings are used here for
; consistency with the other two parameter files.
;===========================================================
;
def eicp_par_lab
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; HOST SAND PARAMETERS
;
; DECLARED ASSUMPTIONS, NOT MEASUREMENTS.
; kappa and lambda are assumptions, not results of this test
; programme:
;   kappa - the unload/reload (US-KL) stage was DROPPED, so no
;           swelling line was measured. Value carried over from
;           Gai & Sanchez (2019) Table 1.
;   lambda - not measurable at the stress levels used here. A
;           normal compression line cannot be identified from
;           triaxial shearing alone; it needs isotropic
;           compression to stresses well beyond pc. Value
;           carried over from Gai & Sanchez Table 1.
; Both must be reported as assumptions in the write-up. They
; are the principal caveat on this validation, exactly as for
; the Kennedy series.
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $kappa_p  = 0.003        ; ASSUMED (US-KL stage dropped)
    $lambda_p = 0.25         ; ASSUMED (not measurable here)
    $ds_p     = 0.04         ; published (Gai Table 1)
    $nu_p     = 0.17         ; published (Gai Table 1)
    $eta_p    = 60.0         ; published (Gai Table 1)
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; CRITICAL STATE SLOPE - M = 1.09 RETAINED
;
; M is NOT calibrated from this test programme, and it cannot
; be: both specimens were STILL SOFTENING at the 20 % axial
; strain termination, with
;     dq/d(epsilon_a) = -3.47 kPa/%  and  -1.29 kPa/%
;
; A specimen still softening has not reached critical state,
; so its stress ratio eta = q/p' is still FALLING toward M.
; The end-of-test eta is therefore an UPPER BOUND on M, not an
; estimate of it. The binding (smallest) upper bound from the
; two specimens is
;     M <= 1.147
;
; The published Gai & Sanchez value M = 1.09 satisfies that
; constraint, so it is retained unchanged. This is a genuine
; consistency check, not a fit: the data constrain M from one
; side only and 1.09 lies inside the admissible range.
;
; REPORT IT AS SUCH. Do not describe 1.147 as a measured M -
; it is a bound. Had 1.09 exceeded it, the published value
; would have been falsified; it does not.
;
; Contrast with the Kennedy series, where phi'_res = 34.43 deg
; was obtained from a specimen at residual with c' = 0, giving
; a genuine measurement of M = 1.393 and a real mismatch.
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $m_cs     = 1.09         ; retained; measured bound M <= 1.147
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; CEMENTATION PARAMETERS - APPLIED BLIND
;
; Published Gai & Sanchez (2019) Table 2 values, calibrated on
; MICP-treated Ottawa sand, applied here WITHOUT adjustment.
; a is the quantity under test in the treated phase: the
; Kennedy series found it over-predicts EICP cementation by a
; factor of about 2.1 at a clean comparison point.
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $a_pa     = 200000.0     ; published - THE QUANTITY UNDER TEST
    $mu_p     = 6.5          ; published
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; INITIAL STATE
;
; e0 is set per specimen by set_case in the driver, from the
; measured value. $ini_e below is only the UDM's internal
; fallback for a zone with no m_e assigned.
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $ini_e    = 0.740        ; fallback; US-100 measured value
    $ini_r    = 0.01         ; fallback; ini_eicp_r recomputes R0
;                              from the actual stress state
    $ini_chi  = 1.0          ; intact bonding at t = 0
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; PRE-CONSOLIDATION PRESSURE - THE SOLE FITTED PARAMETER
;
; pc is the ONLY quantity fitted in this validation. It is
; calibrated against the UNTREATED specimen US-100 alone.
; Everything else is either published (M, Ds, nu, eta, a, mu)
; or a declared assumption (kappa, lambda).
;
; Consequence: every treated run is a PREDICTION, not a fit.
; Do NOT re-tune pc per specimen, per confinement or per
; calcite content. Later confinements, if any, are
; cross-validation of this single value.
;
; TRIAL 1: 460,000 Pa.
; At sigma3 = 100 kPa with mc = 0 (pb = 0) this gives a
; consistent initial sub-loading ratio of
;     R0 = sigma3 / pc = 100000 / 460000 = 0.2174
;
; NOTE on calibrating pc: there is no valid closed-form route
; from a target peak strength to pc. R, pc, chi and the
; dilation response evolve in a coupled way during shearing -
; demonstrated in both parameter directions during the Gai mu
; and a sensitivity studies, and the reason a closed-form
; derivation was rejected for the Kennedy series after it
; overshot by a factor of 3.9. Calibrate by trial, judging
; BOTH peak magnitude AND strain-to-peak.
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $ini_pc_lab = 460000.0   ; TRIAL 1 (Pa) - sole fitted parameter
    $ini_pc     = 460000.0   ; UDM fallback, keep equal to above
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; NUMERICAL GUARDS - identical to the verified Gai set
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $p_min    = 1.0          ; floor on mean effective stress
    $pc_min   = 100.0        ; floor on pre-consolidation press.
    $chi_min  = 1.0e-6       ; floor on damage factor
    $r_min    = 1.0e-6       ; floor on sub-loading ratio
    $r_max    = 1.0          ; ceiling on sub-loading ratio
    $kb_dflt  = 1.0e10       ; default bulk modulus bound (Pa)
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; SUBZONE ACCUMULATORS - volume weighted, reset each zsub cycle
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $m_wt_acc   = 0.0        ; accumulated subzone volume
    $m_vol_acc  = 0.0        ; total volumetric strain
    $m_depv_acc = 0.0        ; plastic volumetric strain
    $m_depq_acc = 0.0        ; plastic deviatoric strain
    $m_dept_acc = 0.0        ; plastic strain norm
    $m_p_acc    = 0.0        ; mean effective stress
    $m_q_acc    = 0.0        ; deviatoric stress
    $m_pls_acc  = 0.0        ; plasticity flag
;
end
;
eicp_par_lab
;
;===========================================================
; EOF
;===========================================================
